Pasta Carbonara Recipe

Ingredients
- 4 egg yolks
- Black pepper (crushed)
- 100g (or more) guanciale (cured pork cheek)
- 200g Pecorino Romano cheese (a whole block, not pre-grated)
- 400g Thick long pasta (like Bucantini)

Instructions
- Cut the guanciale into suitable pieces (thin for crispier, larger for juicyer)
- Fry the guanciale in medium heat for 5-10 minutes. Put aside to cool 
- grate the cheese
- Mix the grated cheese, black pepper and egg yolks into a "chunk"
- Boil the pasta until al-dente. You can add a bit of salt, but it is not needed (Pecorino is really salty). Do NOT drain the pasta.
- Put the pasta into a pan and add some of the water used to boild the pasta.
- Add into the cheese, egg yolk, pepper chunk and mix until even.
- Keep adding the water and mix the pasta until it has a nice smooth creamy texture.
- Add in the guanciale. mix and serve immediatelly. 

